{"id":"NCT03350828","title":"CHaractErizing CFTR Modulated Changes in Sweat Chloride and Their Association With Clinical Outcomes","official":"The CHEC-SC Cohort Study: CHaractErizing CFTR Modulated Changes in Sweat Chloride and Their Association With Clinical Outcomes","summary":"This is a multicenter, cross-sectional, cohort study which will collect contemporary sweat chloride (SC) values from approximately 5000 Cystic Fibrosis (CF) patients prescribed and currently receiving commercially approved Cystic Fibrosis transmembrane conductance regulator (CFTR) modulator therapies.","conditions":["Cystic Fibrosis"],"interventions":[],"criteria":"Inclusion Criteria:\n\n1. Written informed consent (and assent when applicable) obtained from subject or subject's legal representative\n2. Enrolled in the CFFPR\n3. Male or female ≥ 4 months of age on day of study visit\n4. Diagnosis of CF.\n5. Current treatment with a prescribed commercially approved CFTR modulator for at least 90 days prior to enrollment\n6. Able to perform the testing and procedures required for this study, as judged by the investigator\n\nAdditional Inclusion Criteria for CHEC-PKPD Sub-Study:\n\n1. Male or female ≥ 6 years of age on day of study visit.\n2. Current treatment with elexacaftor/tezacaftor/ivacaftor for at least 90 days prior to enrollment.\n3. Last dose of elexacaftor/tezacaftor/ivacaftor taken at least 24hours and last dose of ivacaftor taken at least 12 hours prior to trough blood draw on day of visit.\n\nExclusion Criteria:\n\n1. Presence of a condition or abnormality that, in the opinion of the Investigator, would compromise the safety of the patient or the quality of the data\n2. Currently enrolled in an investigational trial (including open-label follow-on studies and Early Access Programs (EAP) of an agent expected to have an impact on sweat chloride (refer to current list provided on study website)","minAge":"4 Months","maxAge":"","sex":"ALL","healthy":false,"studyType":"OBSERVATIONAL","purpose":"","enrollment":5000,"start":"2018-01-15","pcd":"2026-12-31","upd":"2026-11-23","sponsor":"Nicole Hamblett","areas":["other","rare"],"central":["Olena Boyarska · olena.boyarska@seattlechildrens.org"],"sites":[{"f":"The Children's Hospital Alabama, University of Alabama at Birmingham","city":"Birmingham","pr":"Alabama","zip":"35233","s":"R","lat":33.5207,"lon":-86.8025,"c":"Heather Hathorne · hyhathorne@uabmc.edu"},{"f":"University of Arkansas for Medical Sciences","city":"Little Rock","pr":"Arkansas","zip":"72205","s":"R","lat":34.7465,"lon":-92.2896,"c":"Kathleen Hicks · HicksKathleenT@uams.edu"},{"f":"University of California San Diego","city":"La Jolla","pr":"California","zip":"92093","s":"R","lat":32.8473,"lon":-117.2742,"c":"Gabriel Querido · glquerido@health.ucsd.edu"},{"f":"Childrens Hospital Los Angeles","city":"Los Angeles","pr":"California","zip":"90027","s":"R","lat":34.0522,"lon":-118.2437,"c":"Carmen Reyes · mareyes@chla.usc.edu"},{"f":"Children's Hospital Colorado","city":"Aurora","pr":"Colorado","zip":"80045","s":"R","lat":39.7294,"lon":-104.8319,"c":"Mary Cross · mary.cross@childrenscolorado.org"},{"f":"National Jewish Health","city":"Denver","pr":"Colorado","zip":"80206","s":"R","lat":39.7392,"lon":-104.9847,"c":"Alix Wilson · wilsona@njhealth.org"},{"f":"Yale University School of Medicine","city":"New Haven","pr":"Connecticut","zip":"06520","s":"R","lat":41.3081,"lon":-72.9282,"c":"Marie Egan · marie.egan@yale.edu"},{"f":"University of Florida","city":"Gainesville","pr":"Florida","zip":"32610","s":"R","lat":29.6516,"lon":-82.3248,"c":"Alexa Smith · alexa.howell@ufl.edu"},{"f":"The Nemours Children's Clinic - Orlando","city":"Orlando","pr":"Florida","zip":"32827","s":"R","lat":28.5383,"lon":-81.3792,"c":"Sherry Wooldridge · sherry.wooldridge@nemours.org"},{"f":"Nemours Children's Clinic - Pensacola","city":"Pensacola","pr":"Florida","zip":"32514","s":"R","lat":30.4213,"lon":-87.2169,"c":"Rebecca Davis · Rebecca.Davis@nemours.org"},{"f":"Ch